# Context Routing Map ([PROJECT_NAME])

Read when: always at session start. Skip when: never.

Start with only `AI_AGENT.md`, `docs/SESSION_BRIEF.md`, `docs/CONTEXT_ROUTING.md`. Pull deeper docs only on triggers.

## Doc Triggers

| Doc | Load when |
|---|---|
| `docs/PROJECT_CANVAS.md` | scope, milestone, or next action unclear |
| `docs/ENGINEERING_PLAYBOOK.md` | commands, test policy, workflow matrix, smoke catalog, review, DoD |
| `docs/TECH_STACK.md` | architecture, dependency, integration boundary |
| `docs/MASTER_TRACEABILITY_TABLE.md` | entrypoint, workflow, side effect, smoke evidence |
| `docs/OPS_SECURITY_RELEASE.md` | deploy, secrets, auth, logging, data, release |
| `docs/TEMPLATE_LIFECYCLE.md` | install, retrofit, missing capability, ignored script, profiles, placeholders, upgrade |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | behavior history or documenting a change |
| `AI_CONTEXT.md` | local reads are insufficient and generated map exists |

## Event Triggers

| Event | Load / Run |
|---|---|
| Version/release/bump | run the project bump script (see `docs/ENGINEERING_PLAYBOOK.md` §1) |
| Merge/predeploy | `scripts/predeploy_full_suite.sh` |
| Behavior change lacks docs | `scripts/enforce_doc_updates.sh` |
| Template version bump | `scripts/check_template_drift.sh` + `docs/TEMPLATE_LIFECYCLE.md` §7 |
| New entrypoint/workflow | `docs/MASTER_TRACEABILITY_TABLE.md` + `docs/ENGINEERING_PLAYBOOK.md` §3 |
| New smoke test | `docs/ENGINEERING_PLAYBOOK.md` §4 |
| BUGFIX | `docs/ENGINEERING_PLAYBOOK.md` test policy (§2) |
| Install/retrofit/migration | `docs/TEMPLATE_LIFECYCLE.md` §2 and §4 |
| Existing lean project audit | `docs/TEMPLATE_LIFECYCLE.md` "Lean project audit" |
| Session brief has `(not set)` | `docs/GAME_PLAN.md` + `scripts/sync_session_brief.sh` |
| Multi-service or release-prep repo | `docs/TEMPLATE_LIFECYCLE.md` §4.2 |
| Beta/user acceptance | `docs/MASTER_TRACEABILITY_TABLE.md` + `docs/ENGINEERING_PLAYBOOK.md` §3 |
| Optional/skipped runtime smoke | `scripts/test_smoke.sh` + `docs/ENGINEERING_PLAYBOOK.md` §2 |
| Security docs promise scan | compare ops docs, CI, `scripts/verify.sh` |

If event is unlisted and unclear, ask. If more than three deeper docs seem needed before first edit, ask whether task is too broad.

## Skip Rules
- Skip `CHANGELOG.md` for routine implementation unless documenting the change.
- Skip `OPS_SECURITY_RELEASE.md` for isolated local/test-only work.
- Skip `MASTER_TRACEABILITY_TABLE.md` for Tier A doc-only edits with no runtime pathway.
- Skip `TECH_STACK.md` when the task is local and architecture is already clear.
